  "body": "Stacked on #782 (E1, `issue/637-carried-stock-field`). Until #782 merges, this diff also shows E1's commit. This PR's own change is the last commit.\n\n## What changed\n\n#637 step E2a, route (ii) of the [step-E design](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/637#issuecomment-6787218007).\n\n- `SdfField::turned(&LatticeTurn) -> (SdfField, Point3)` (new `field_turn.rs`) bakes the turn's signed permutation into the data and returns the translation as the residual view. Brick `b` maps to `!b` (`== -b-1`, total on `i32`, so it can't overflow and there is no failure arm) on a negated axis, with the slot mirrored (`s -> 7 - s`). Axes are swapped on a quarter turn. Band bricks, cuts, `cut_ups` and `cut_downs` are re-indexed and never re-sampled. Shell facets and the closed-form box are negated or swapped exactly.\n- New `cut_downs` layer on `SdfField`, the mirror of `cut_ups`. On a flip the two maps trade places: the swap is the record. Nothing reads it yet (E2b).\n- A flipped bake that has cuts sets `bounded_cuts`. The E1 monotone floor law assumes cuts came from above, so until E2b's up-march exists, a floor a cut came near is refused by name (`CutFromBelow`).\n- Cost ledger: `full` is re-keyed, `region` is rebuilt, and every cut brick is marked dirty (the ledger stays a superset of what moved).\n- `LatticeTurn::shift()` (pub) and `linear()` (crate) accessors.\n- `field.rs` split by the 400-line law. The input gate (`validate_shell`, `edge_key` and their tests) moved to `field_shell.rs` and is re-exported. `field.rs` goes from 467 to 340 lines.\n- Decisions are in `docs/decisions/779-field-turn-bake.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `field_carry::a_baked_turn_reads_bit_for_bit_what_the_view_reads`: for all 8 turns, on a block field (closed-form box plus a slot) and on a mesh-seeded field (band bricks plus a ball slot), `turned(t).0.distance(p - shift)`, `mesh_distance` and `inside` are bit-identical to `CarriedField::new(f, t)`. The stated scope is points off the lattice planes and off the shell's crossings.\n- `carry_engine_agreement::a_baked_turn_reads_what_the_view_reads_through_every_turn`: covers the top slot, the through-slot, the floor sliver and the off-grid ball slot. For all 8 turns, the distance at every column centre of the carried lattice, at each cell-centre height, is bit-identical. For the 4 upright turns, the whole `column_body` read-back (tops, floors, `empty_at`, `floor_judged`) is bit-identical too. A mutation check (slot mirror removed) makes this test fail.\n- Unit tests in `field_turn`: four quarter turns restore every layer, the mesh, `region` and `full` bit for bit. A flip moves each `cut_ups` record to the mirrored cell's `cut_downs` and back again, and sets `bounded_cuts`. A bake marks every cut brick dirty, and an upright bake leaves `bounded_cuts` unset.\n- Quick gate green (27 sim suites incl. `stock_backend_parity`, `stock_carry`; motion `posed_subtract`; app `stock_export`, `verify`; 2.3 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -D warnings` is clean. The Linux batch gate is running.\n- Column-engine verdicts, goldens and snapshots are unchanged. No existing test was edited apart from gate-map header lines.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The column read-back of a **flipped** bake. Its floor under a cut needs E2b's `march_up` reading `cut_downs`, and until then it refuses by name. This PR pins only the flipped bake's distance.\n- No caller uses `turned` yet. E2c (`CarriedField::simulate`) is the first. The view (`CarriedField`) stays the carried read.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.16.0\n\nFixes #779\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
